Please find attached my small example with the bam, saf and bed files.
featureCoutns was used as follows:

featureCounts --minReadOverlap 1 -Q 1 -T 12 -a ../matrix_gene_protein_coding.saf -F SAF -O -o K27ac_WEN1_ch1_reg_total_counts.txt K27ac_WEN1_ch1_reg.sort.bam

head K27ac_WEN1_ch1_reg_total_counts.txt.summary
Status K27ac_WEN1_ch1_reg.sort.bam
Assigned 7617

awk '{count = count + $7} END{print count}' K27ac_WEN1_ch1_reg_total_counts.txt
7617

samtools view -c -q 1 -F 4 -L ../matrix_gene_protein_coding.bed K27ac_WEN1_ch1_reg.sort.bam
7615

So, there were no overlapping regions because assigned reads in K27ac_WEN1_ch1_reg_total_counts.txt.summary and sum of reads in K27ac_WEN1_ch1_reg_total_counts.txt gave the same number (7617).
Samtools output is still 7615.

